* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
* jank mini 2.2, LINE IN front end (README "LINE IN", "stage 2"): the circuit as in parts.py, shared by the runs in
* linein.py. Models are GENERIC, not the vendors' own:
*  - OPAMP: LMV321 by its datasheet figures (TI SLOS263Y, VCC 2.7 V table): 1 MHz unity gain (one pole), 100 dB DC gain,
*    output to within 60 mV (low) / 20 mV (high) of the rails, 40 ohm output; its own supply rejection not modelled
*    (the datasheet's PSRR is 60 dB or more: the supply's path through the bias divider below is the larger one).
*  - TVS: SMAJ5.0CA per line (stage 1e) as two 6.4 V zeners back to back, 2 nF (ASSUMED: Hongjiacheng's sheet gives no
*    capacitance; 400 W SMA TVS parts of 5 V are 1 .. 4 nF), its leakage modelled by the diodes only.
*  - LDO (U7, XC6206P332MR on VSYS): AVDD = min(3.3 V, VSYS - 0.2 V) plus the input ripple x 10^(-PSRR/20), PSRR = 50 dB
*    (ASSUMED: Torex's sheet gives a ripple-rejection curve, not re-read here; 50 dB at 1 kHz is a typical figure for this
*    class), a 1 uF output cap (C35).
*  - ADC: the pin as a switched sampling capacitor CS (Espressif publishes no value: ASSUMED 10 pF, reset to 0 V before
*    every sample, the worst case), closed for TACQ every sample period.
*  - J7's ring switch (pin 3): closed to the ring with no plug (LCSC's PJ-307C drawing; to check with a meter), a 0.03
*    ohm contact (the sheet's maximum).

.subckt OPAMP inp inn out vcc vee
G1 0 n1 inp inn 1m
R1 n1 0 100Meg
C1 n1 0 159p
Bl n2 0 V = min(max(V(n1), V(vee) + 0.06), V(vcc) - 0.02)
Rout n2 out 40
.ends

.model DZ64 D(BV=6.4 IBV=1m CJO=2n)
.subckt TVS line gnd
D1 line mid DZ64
D2 gnd mid DZ64
.ends

* U7: AVDD from VSYS (ripple scaled by the PSRR; DC follows VSYS when VSYS is under 3.5 V)
.subckt LDO vin out gnd psrr_db=50
Bdc dc gnd V = min(3.3, V(vin) - 0.2)
Clp vin2 gnd 1
Rlp vin vin2 1Meg
Bout o2 gnd V = V(dc) + (V(vin) - V(vin2)) * pow(10, -{psrr_db} / 20)
Ro o2 out 0.5
C35 out gnd 1u
.ends

* the front end: tip / ring / sleeve in, AIN = the ADC pin (GPIO9); R36 / R37 the stage-2 pull-downs (rpd: 100k fitted,
* 1e12 left out); stage 2 (the user's ground loops): the sleeve to GND through R39 (22 ohm) and, through R65 10 k / R66
* 5.6 k (k = 5.6 / 15.6 = R32 / (R32 + R30 / 2): the summer's own ratio), into the bias's return, C33 and R34: a voltage
* between the sleeve and GND then reaches the op-amp's + input as much as its two inputs pass it to the output, and cancels
* (gs=1; gs=0: stage 1f's front end, the sleeve on GND, C33 1 uF)
.subckt FRONTEND tip ring ain avdd gnd slv rpd=100k gs=1 cb=1e-18
XD7 tip gnd TVS
XD8 ring gnd TVS
R36 tip gnd {rpd}
R37 ring gnd {rpd}
R39 slv gnd {gs > 0.5 ? 22 : 1e-3}
R65 slv gsn {gs > 0.5 ? 10e3 : 1e12}
R66 gsn gnd {gs > 0.5 ? 5.6e3 : 1e-3}
C67 gsn gnd {cb}
R30 tip a1 20k
C30 a1 inn 1u
R31 ring a2 20k
C31 a2 inn 1u
R32 inn out 5.6k
C32 inn out 2.2n
R33 avdd vb 150k
R34 vb gsn 120k
C33 vb gsn {gs > 0.5 ? 220n : 1u}
XU6 vb inn out avdd gnd OPAMP
R35 out ain 120
C36 ain gnd 100n
.ends
